---
layout: base.njk
home: true
title: null
description: The open framework for AI-native companies — a shared space where teams think out loud and agents do the work, reachable over any channel, on infrastructure you own.
---
<section class="lp-hero">
  <div class="lp-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="lp-container lp-hero-inner">
    <span class="lp-eyebrow">Open source · Clojure &amp; Nix</span>
    <h1 class="lp-title">The framework for<br /><span class="lp-grad">AI-native companies</span></h1>
    <p class="lp-sub">
      Describe your company's processes as deterministic Lisp, let an always-on
      orchestrator spawn ephemeral agents for the parts that need judgement, and
      run all of it on infrastructure you own.
    </p>
    <div class="lp-cta-row">
      <a class="lp-btn lp-btn-primary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
      <a class="lp-btn lp-btn-ghost" href="{{ site.github }}" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
    </div>
    <ul class="lp-chips">
      <li>Deterministic processes</li>
      <li>Capability-scoped agents</li>
      <li>Talk over any channel</li>
      <li>Self-hosted</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-lede">
  <div class="lp-container">
    <p>
      An AI-native company runs on agents. Reflection makes them
      <strong>trustworthy</strong>: deterministic processes, capability-scoped
      agents, and infrastructure you own — top to bottom, open source.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section">
  <div class="lp-container">
    <h2 class="lp-h2">Agents belong to the team, not to a tab</h2>
    <p class="lp-section-lead">
      The personal-agent model breaks the moment a team moves fast. Reflection
      is built on the opposite bet.
    </p>
    <div class="lp-shift-grid">
      <div class="lp-shift-card lp-shift-old">
        <div class="lp-shift-label">The old way</div>
        <p>
          Everyone drives their own agent in their own tab, then merges the
          results by hand. At speed it falls apart — divergent context,
          duplicated work, and conflicts nobody asked to reconcile.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-shift-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
      <div class="lp-shift-card lp-shift-new">
        <div class="lp-shift-label">With Reflection</div>
        <p>
          People think out loud and decide together in one shared space. Agents
          live in that same context — reading the same discussion, writing to
          the same knowledge base — and do the work in the open. Team agents,
          not personal ones. Nothing to merge.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section">
  <div class="lp-container">
    <h2 class="lp-h2">One stack, top to bottom</h2>
    <p class="lp-section-lead">
      From the channel you already use, down to the metal you own.
    </p>
    <div class="lp-stack">
      <div class="lp-tier lp-tier-comms">
        <div class="lp-tier-name">Communication</div>
        <div class="lp-tier-desc">
          The shared space. People discuss and decide over the channel they
          already use — Discourse, Zulip, Telegram, GitHub issues, email — and
          agents live in that same context.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-conn">↕ messages in · answers out</div>
      <div class="lp-tier lp-tier-zeno">
        <div class="lp-tier-name"><span>zeno</span> — orchestration</div>
        <div class="lp-tier-desc">
          Deterministic processes in Lisp spawn ephemeral, capability-scoped
          agents. An agent can ask the team and resume when the reply lands —
          over that same channel.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-conn">↑ runs on</div>
      <div class="lp-tier lp-tier-nixops">
        <div class="lp-tier-name"><span>nixops</span> — infrastructure</div>
        <div class="lp-tier-desc">
          Your servers as code: reproducible, rollback-safe, self-hosted from
          the metal up.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section">
  <div class="lp-container">
    <h2 class="lp-h2">The stack</h2>
    <p class="lp-section-lead">Open-source building blocks. Start with one; grow into the rest.</p>
    <div class="lp-pillar-grid">
      {% for project in site.projects %}
        <article class="lp-pillar">
          <div class="lp-pillar-icon">
            {% if project.slug == "zeno" %}
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" /><circle cx="12" cy="3.6" r="1.6" /><circle cx="4.3" cy="18" r="1.6" /><circle cx="19.7" cy="18" r="1.6" /><path d="M12 9V5.2M10.2 13.7 6 16.6M13.8 13.7 18 16.6" /></svg>
            {% elif project.slug == "nixops" %}
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3.5" y="4" width="17" height="6" rx="1.5" /><rect x="3.5" y="14" width="17" height="6" rx="1.5" /><path d="M7 7h.01M7 17h.01" /></svg>
            {% else %}
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8" /></svg>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
          <div class="lp-pillar-role">{{ project.role }}</div>
          <h3>{{ project.name }}</h3>
          <p>{{ project.tagline }}</p>
          <div class="lp-pillar-links">
            {% if project.docs %}<a href="{{ project.docs }}">Docs →</a>{% endif %}
            <a href="{{ project.repo }}" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section">
  <div class="lp-container">
    <h2 class="lp-h2">Principles</h2>
    <p class="lp-section-lead">The beliefs the whole stack is built on.</p>
    <div class="lp-principle-grid">
      <div class="lp-principle">
        <h4>One shared context</h4>
        <p>Work happens in a space the whole team sees, not in private tabs. Agents read and write the same context, so there is nothing to merge.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-principle">
        <h4>Deterministic by default</h4>
        <p>Processes are explicit Lisp. An agent is called only where no deterministic practice exists yet — not for everything.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-principle">
        <h4>Security by design</h4>
        <p>Security is structural, not bolted on. Every agent gets its own auto-generated MCP exposing a deny-by-default capability grant — secrets stay in the orchestrator, and a prompt injection can't reach what was never granted.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-principle">
        <h4>Meet humans where they are</h4>
        <p>Communication is separated from work. An agent asks the team over whatever channel you already use — chat, Telegram, GitHub issues, email — and resumes when the answer lands.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-principle">
        <h4>Own your stack</h4>
        <p>Self-hosted from the metal up. Your processes, your data, your servers — no platform in the middle.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-cta-band">
  <div class="lp-container lp-cta-inner">
    <h2>Build a company that runs itself.</h2>
    <p>Start with the orchestrator and grow the stack from there.</p>
    <div class="lp-cta-row">
      <a class="lp-btn lp-btn-primary" href="/docs/zeno/">Start with zeno</a>
      <a class="lp-btn lp-btn-ghost" href="{{ site.github }}" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
